VortX patch 0004: let the moltenvk render context notice that its layer resized.

WHY THIS EXISTS
---------------
video/out/vulkan/context_moltenvk.m is NOT an upstream mpv file. It is 96 lines invented by
MPVKit's own 0001-player-add-moltenvk-context.patch, and it is the render context every Apple
device on the libmpv lane draws through. It shipped as the thinnest thing that compiles:
`struct ra_ctx_params params = {0}` (all seven capability hooks null) and a `control` that
answers VO_NOTIMPL to every request.

The cost of that stub landed in the app. Because nothing could tell mpv the CAMetalLayer had
changed size, a device rotation, a macOS window resize or a background/foreground cycle left the
swapchain and vo->dwidth/dheight on the OLD geometry, and the video stayed small in a corner.
The only lever the host app had was to destroy and rebuild the entire decode plus VO chain
(`vid=no` then `vid=auto`) on every single layout change. This patch removes the need for that.

WHAT IT DOES
------------
Handles VOCTRL_CHECK_EVENTS, which mpv's vo thread already polls once per loop iteration
(video/out/vo.c). It compares the layer's drawableSize against the size the swapchain was last
built for, and on a real change resizes the swapchain and raises VO_EVENT_RESIZE. vo_gpu_next
then recomputes the source/destination rects and the OSD resolution from the fresh
vo->dwidth/dheight and requests a redraw.

The resize is done in the control itself, matching context_mac.m, and that is not a style
choice: vo_gpu_next's reaction to VO_EVENT_RESIZE is gpu_ctx_resize(), which is an explicit
no-op on the Vulkan path ("vulkan RA handles this by itself"), so raising the event without
resizing here would change nothing at all.

Deliberately NOT in this patch: set_color / preferred_csp (P2), get_vsync (P3), check_visible
and preferred_ref_luma (P4). Those are separate, larger, and P2 in particular rests on an
unproven hypothesis about the target-colorspace-hint double free. Kept small so it is provable.

CONFLICT RISK
-------------
Structurally near zero. Upstream mpv ships no file at this path, so no upstream bump can
conflict with it. It does depend on MPVKit's 0001 patch having created the file, so it must
sort AFTER 0001 in Sources/BuildScripts/patch/libmpv/ (SpikeGit.applyPatches applies that
directory in sorted order).

--- a/video/out/vulkan/context_moltenvk.m
+++ b/video/out/vulkan/context_moltenvk.m
@@ -26,6 +26,12 @@
 struct priv {
     struct mpvk_ctx vk;
     CAMetalLayer *layer;
+    // VortX: the drawableSize we last sized the swapchain against, in pixels. moltenvk_control
+    // compares the layer against THIS rather than against ctx->vo->dwidth/dheight, because
+    // pl_swapchain_resize is allowed to clamp the size it is handed and write the clamped value
+    // back into vo->dwidth. Comparing against a clamped value would never match the layer again,
+    // so every VOCTRL_CHECK_EVENTS would raise a resize and spin the vo thread at 100%.
+    int last_width, last_height;
 };
 
 static void moltenvk_uninit(struct ra_ctx *ctx)
@@ -73,16 +79,61 @@
     return false;
 }
 
+// VortX: single place that resizes the swapchain and remembers what it was sized to, so
+// moltenvk_reconfig and moltenvk_control can never disagree about the current size.
+static bool moltenvk_resize(struct ra_ctx *ctx, int width, int height)
+{
+    struct priv *p = ctx->priv;
+    p->last_width = width;
+    p->last_height = height;
+    return ra_vk_ctx_resize(ctx, width, height);
+}
+
 static bool moltenvk_reconfig(struct ra_ctx *ctx)
 {
     struct priv *p = ctx->priv;
     CGSize s = p->layer.drawableSize;
-    ra_vk_ctx_resize(ctx, s.width, s.height);
+    moltenvk_resize(ctx, (int)s.width, (int)s.height);
     return true;
 }
 
 static int moltenvk_control(struct ra_ctx *ctx, int *events, int request, void *arg)
 {
+    struct priv *p = ctx->priv;
+
+    switch (request) {
+    // VortX: this context has no windowing backend to deliver events, so nothing ever told mpv
+    // that the CAMetalLayer changed size. A device rotation or a window resize left the swapchain
+    // (and vo->dwidth/dheight, which feed vo_get_src_dst_rects) on the OLD geometry, and the video
+    // stayed small in a corner. The only way the host app could make mpv notice was to destroy and
+    // rebuild the whole decode plus VO chain (vid=no then vid=auto). Poll the layer here instead:
+    // it is the same size source moltenvk_reconfig already trusts, and it is the idiom
+    // context_mac.m uses (raise VO_EVENT_RESIZE, then resize the swapchain from the control).
+    //
+    // The resize must happen HERE. vo_gpu_next's own resize() reacts to VO_EVENT_RESIZE by calling
+    // gpu_ctx_resize(), which is an explicit no-op on the Vulkan path ("vulkan RA handles this by
+    // itself", video/out/gpu_next/context.c), so raising the event alone would change nothing.
+    case VOCTRL_CHECK_EVENTS: {
+        CGSize s = p->layer.drawableSize;
+        int w = (int)s.width, h = (int)s.height;
+        // MoltenVK momentarily forces drawableSize to 1x1 to complete a presentation (mpv PR
+        // 13651). Never rebuild the swapchain against that transient value: the host app's
+        // CAMetalLayer subclass rejects it on the way in for the same reason.
+        if (w <= 1 || h <= 1)
+            return VO_TRUE;
+        if (w == p->last_width && h == p->last_height)
+            return VO_TRUE;
+        if (!moltenvk_resize(ctx, w, h))
+            return VO_ERROR;
+        // Deliberate: this is the only externally observable proof that the poll fired, and the
+        // host app already forwards mpv log messages at verbose level, so it is also the field
+        // evidence that a rotation was handled without rebuilding the video chain.
+        MP_VERBOSE(ctx, "moltenvk: layer resized to %dx%d\n", w, h);
+        *events |= VO_EVENT_RESIZE;
+        return VO_TRUE;
+    }
+    }
+
     return VO_NOTIMPL;
 }
 
